## Tools

`config/toolchain.json` pins every tool this project downloads: URL, sha256,
version, license and where the bytes came from. `configure.py` fetches them into
`build/tools/` with `tools/download_tool.py` (standard library only), checking the
sha256 before anything is extracted or run. romwright itself downloads nothing.

* `binutils-arm-none-eabi` is the Arm GNU Toolchain (GCC and binutils, GPL); the
  project only runs `as`, `ld`, `objcopy` and `cpp` from it.
* `agbcc` is the `pret/agbcc` release binary (GCC 2.95-derived, GPL; the release
  has no license file of its own). Nintendo's AGB SDK headers in it are
  Nintendo's. Use it only if you are entitled to.
* To use tools you already have, write a toolchain profile (JSON, the format in
  romwright's `docs/toolchains.md`) and pass `python3 configure.py --toolchain profile.json`,
  or save it as `config/toolchain.local.json` (ignored by git). The tool keys are
  `as`, `ld`, `objcopy`, `cpp`, `compiler` (agbcc) and `objdiff-cli`.

## Decompiling a function

Every function is its own `asm/main/NNNN/<name>.s` ({{ASM_UNITS}} of them), in
GNU `as` unified syntax, with its literal pool as labelled `.4byte`s. To replace one
with C:

```sh
python3 configure.py swap <name-or-0xADDRESS> [--src my_function.c]
# edit src/main/NNNN/<name>.c until `ninja` is green again
```

`swap` turns the unit's entry in `config/units.json` from `asm` into `c`; the next
`ninja` compiles it (cpp, then agbcc, then `as`) and links its `.text` into the
same slot. A C unit that is longer than its slot stops the link ("cannot move
location counter backwards"); literals and data it emits are not linked (the retail
bytes are already in the ROM), so it can only name symbols by `extern`.
`include/romwright_types.h` has the base types and `include/romwright_protos.h` the
prototypes romwright recovered. `objdiff.json` lists every C unit with its retail
target object; `ninja progress` writes `build/report.json`.

## Layout

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `config/units.json` | the whole ROM as units: header, asm functions, data ranges, C units |
| `config/symbols.txt` | names, addresses, sizes and modes romwright recovered |
| `config/symbols.ld` | absolute names for data no object defines |
| `config/header.json` | cartridge header fields; `tools/header.py` writes `asm/header.s` and computes the complement check |
| `config/checksum.sha1` | the retail sha1 `ninja` checks against |
| `config/project.json` | project facts: image, compiler evidence and flags |
| `include/` | base types, recovered prototypes, assembly macros |
| `src/` | your C units |
| `decompiled/` | optional non-matching reference C from romwright (`--decompile`), not built |
